  With 4 kids living at home, and paying 5 tuitions?  I would never be
able to self-justify the expense.  (read: "I'm cheap")  Not to mention
I have no idea what I'd converse about, captive in a house/hotel full
of lojbanists for a XX-hour period.  I'm pretty introverted.  I can't
make small talk in English, I doubt I could do it in lojban.  :-(  I
mean, it's SO weird, I can say pretty much say anything I want to say
in lojban, but then I find.... I don't really have anything to say.
My favorite activities lojban-wise is translating what random people
in the hallway or on the radio say... Like, I fantasize about trekking
out to lojbab's house (he lives about an hour or two drive away),
meeting him, and saying "coi lojbab .i ioro'a do finti la lojban .i lo
nu penmi do cu pluka .i yyyy  mi mo'u tavla do . i co'o", getting back
in my car and driving back for 1-2 hous.  Cause I have a feeling
that's pretty much how it would go.  Heck, that's how it DID go (in
English analogue)  when I met my fellow Washington Post Style
Invitational Losers at their annual party.


                 --gejyspa

